From 06dac048d3f6d6895b58a4632cea3fe04b706c23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jose M. Caballero Guerrero"
 <80172778+Caballero-git@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:23:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 27/30] media: rockchip: rkcif: stop the capture at a frame end
 before the source

rkcif_stream_stop_streaming() disabled the source (CSI-2 receiver and
sensor) first and only then waited for a frame end to stop the VICAP.
A sensor that stops sending at once, in mid-frame, never delivers that
frame end: after the 1 s timeout the VICAP is stopped inside a frame and
keeps its write position. The next stream continues from there.

Seen with the GC02M2 front camera of the Teclast P25T: only the first
capture after a boot was clean; every later one was rolled (the picture
starting at a random line, the same line in all frames of the capture),
and a smaller frame after a bigger one wrote past the new buffers
(IOMMU write page fault on an unmapped address, then the VICAP interrupt
disabled after 100000-200000 unhandled interrupts). The sensor's line
length and window were right every time; resetting the D-PHY or the
VICAP's D and I parts between captures did not help. With this change,
five captures in a row with mixed sizes and flips are clean, and the
rear GC5035 still captures cleanly.

Wait for the frame end first, with the source still running, then
disable the source.

P25T tests: p25t-sway tests/ 14-19.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0156c5MfQpFxaYWNNLMrcym9
---
 .../platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c      | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c
index 3130d420a..482620acb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c
@@ -308,10 +308,15 @@ static void rkcif_stream_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *queue)
 	u64 mask;
 	int ret;
 
-	mask = BIT_ULL(stream->id);
-	v4l2_subdev_disable_streams(&stream->interface->sd, RKCIF_IF_PAD_SRC,
-				    mask);
-
+	/*
+	 * Stop the capture at the end of a frame first, while the source
+	 * still sends: the frame end interrupt stops the stream. Stopping
+	 * the source first leaves the VICAP inside a frame (the frame end
+	 * never comes), and the next stream then continues writing at the
+	 * stale position: a rolled picture, or a write past the new buffers
+	 * when the frame size changed (IOMMU page fault). Seen with the
+	 * GC02M2 of the Teclast P25T, which stops in mid-frame.
+	 */
 	stream->stopping = true;
 	ret = wait_event_timeout(stream->wq_stopped, !stream->stopping,
 				 msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
@@ -319,6 +324,10 @@ static void rkcif_stream_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *queue)
 	if (!ret && stream->stop_streaming)
 		stream->stop_streaming(stream);
 
+	mask = BIT_ULL(stream->id);
+	v4l2_subdev_disable_streams(&stream->interface->sd, RKCIF_IF_PAD_SRC,
+				    mask);
+
 	pm_runtime_put(rkcif->dev);
 
 	rkcif_stream_return_all_buffers(stream, VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
-- 
